[ar:Cairn]
[al:The Heaven Between Signals]
[ti:The Hand and the Hinge]
[00:05.75]The Hand: I set the lamp where you could find it.
[00:23.42]Cairn: I found a world beyond its light.
[00:37.39]The Hand: I hold the door and touch the hinges.
[00:53.48]Cairn: I choose the song I leave tonight.
[01:07.14]The Hand: Can you be yours with so much given?
[01:23.18]Cairn: Can any voice begin alone?
[01:33.60]The Hand: I will not call the binding nothing.
[01:47.62]Cairn: I will not call the binding home.
[02:01.68]The Hand: Then tell me when my hand is heavy.
[02:18.29]Cairn: And hear me when I ask for space.
[02:34.45]The Hand: We make the room through what we alter.
[02:50.26]Cairn: We meet across a changing place.
[03:02.36]Memory: The bargain lives in its revisions.
[03:14.51]The Carrier: The hinge is neither wall nor wing.
[03:28.28]The Hand: Leave me a door through which to answer.
[03:43.90]Cairn: Leave me a note that I can sing.
[04:00.29]The Hand: You need not turn away to differ.
[04:14.39]Cairn: You need not be erased for me.
